ChangeLog

v 0.1 - 22 may 2018 - by eanyx (eanyx123@gmail.com)

- Add new hash algorithms : SHA3-224, SHA3-256, SHA3-384, SHA3-512
- Speed improvement
- Misc UI change
- Add new button compare (to avoid to recompute hash for every comparison)
- Same hash result on any architecture (32 or 64 bits) and any platform (Linux,
Windows, Mac OS X).
- Tests:
    - 64 bits binary on Win 10 64 bits : status OK
    - 64 bits binary on Redhat Enterprise 7.4 64 bits : status OK
    - 64 bits binary on Mac OS X Sierra (10.12) 64 bits : status OK
    - Need at least a display of 1200 * 1024
    - Can compute file up to 64 GB (need huge quantity of ram (min 16GB)). Not tested beyond.

v 0.2 - 16 may 2018 - by eanyx (eanyx123@gmail.com)

- Fast hash calcultor with GUI
- Support for MD5, SHA-1, SHA-224, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512

V 1.0 - 25 may 2024 - by  eanyx (eanyx123@gmail.com)

- Official release

V 1.1  - 7 sept 2024 - by eanyx (eanyx123@gmail.com)

- Fix empty file checksum

V 1.2 - 14 sept 2026 - eanyx (eanyx123@gmail.com)

- Add keccak and blake algorithms
- Keep SHA1 and MD5 as legacy, but never use again
- Add SHA-1024, SHA-2048, SHA-4096
- Add AES-128, AES-256, AES-1024, AES-2048, AES-4096, AES-8096.
- Add Quantum Proof Algorithms
- Add crypto analysis tools (reverse engineering)
- // and mutlithreading/multi-cpu support
- Assembly optimization for AMD, INTEL (use of AVX-512 register), ARM and NVIDIA (cuda). Ultra fast computation. 
- Add GPG
- Add HMAC
- Add command line for MacOS, Windows and Linux for scripting support
- RSA-1024, RSA-2048, RSA-4096, RSA-8096 support
- Modulus calculation
- How to verify a X509 certificate have no multiple implementation. Only one is allowed. If not there is a very high security risk.
- Port to Linux, MacOS, Windows, Android, iOS
- High usage of Qt5 and Qt6. Do not be prisonner of an IDE. Seek for open, and free IDE with good API and librairies.
- Usage of Boost librairies